jd:
The course program is designed for students of technical specialties of universities, beginners in software development, those who have completed specialized courses and have a basic knowledge of any programming language. If you have experience in Java, .NET, Python, but no experience in Ruby - that's okay, we will help you acquire it. The main thing is the desire to learn the theory of Ruby and work it out in practice. If this is about you - we are glad to invite you to study!

With us, you will receive not only "dry" theory, but also practice in real Ruby projects that will help you get your first job in IT or change your current specialty.
The training is free of charge, with a scholarship. The set is open.

**REQUIREMENTS FOR CANDIDATES:**
- understanding of OOP;
- experience with JS, HTML, CSS;
- experience with SQL / PostgresSQL / MySQL;
- experience with Git;
- independence and focus on results;
- the ability to search for the necessary information;
- teamwork skills;
- English Intermediate and higher (important!)

**FOR START:**
- send your CV;
- take a short interview in English over the phone;
- take the test assignment and technical interview and get positive feedback;
- own a laptop.

**EDUCATION SYSTEM:**
- 3 months of training (can be reduced to 2 months depending on the initial level and academic performance), those who have passed it will be accepted for a trial period at the company;
- format: full-time training 40 hours per  week.

**WHAT YOU GET:**
- a mentor with the commercial products experience who will lead you the way;
- a course that costs more than $ 1000 - you will get it for free!
- you will be involved in real projects;
- a wonderful team of young professionals, opportunities for professional development, corporate English lessons and communication with native speakers, English Days.
- During the training, you will perform practical tasks, on the basis of the verification of which the knowledge gained will be assessed. The final stage is an interview, after successful completion of which you will receive the position of Junior Ruby on Rails Developer at Gotoinc.

**And finally, WHY RUBY:**
1. You get all the comforts (pleasure) without gimmicks.
Ruby borrows all the best from other programming languages, from smalltalk to Java, from Perl to Python.
2. You will love the little things.
Ruby is graceful. Why? Because he does not try to make the code laconic enough to interfere with readability and understanding.
3. No need to use semicolon anymore.
4. You can change the environment in any way you can.
5. XML - really not needed.
6. You use only those libraries and modules that are necessary.
7. There are many useful libraries that are ready to use (Ruby Gems).
8. Lambda is more than just a Greek letter.
9. Large and friendly community :)
10. You can use Rails. Last but not least ... You can always use Rails to develop web applications. Development will not be as easy as PHP, but Rails was written in Ruby because it has features not found in other languages.

We are waiting for your CV!

