Company Description

Arrible specializes in full-cycle game production, VR design and development, and art outsourcing services. 
We have a variety of professionals including game artists, Unity, and Unreal developers, game designers, and testers. 
And now Arrible invites a Technical artist 3D to be part of our creative team.

🎮 Requirements:

• 2+ years in the game industry as a technical artist;
• Expert knowledge of Photoshop, 3D modeling tools;
• Unity experience;
• Strong understanding of the modern artistic toolset and rendering pipelines (Forward/Deferred Shading, Ambient Occlusion, etc..)
• Experience in a full digital art content creation pipeline;
Good technical art background;
• Independent creative learner with a passion for making games;
• A team player with good verbal communication skills;
• Experience in writing shaders for Unity projects will be a huge plus;
• Intermediate English will be a plus;
• Portfolio will be a huge plus.

🎮 What additional skills will help you:

• Experience with scripting languages;
• Technical expertise with the standard industry toolset;
• Knowledge Maya, Blender, etc.;
• Experience with version control systems (Git, SVN, Perforce, etc.);
• Experience with CPU/GPU Unity Profiling Tools will be a plus.

Additional Information

🎮 Extra goodies that await you at Arrible:

•  We work exclusively remotely. Once a quarter - corporate events in Kyiv or Odesa.
•  Another bonus - we do not have time tracking and other micromanagement, typical of "galleys". All on trust.
•  Every month you have +2 days off. Thus, 24 vacation days are accumulated per year. Spend them whenever you want.
•  Interesting and varied projects: after all, we are outsourcing, and we are also a developer and publisher of our own games.
•  Development within the company: 
   ✔ Firstly, our "oldies" 7 years ago were doing what is "in trend" now, there is a lot to learn from each other.
   ✔ And secondly, we are the creators of the best VR game of the year.

