Project Overview:
A US based automotive startup with the goal to provide aftermarket V2X technology. It will address the 300 million vehicles on U.S. roads (private cars and commercial fleets). The main goal is to save lives and costs associated with traffic incidents, reduce lost productivity due to traffic congestion and reduce fuel waste and CO2 footprint. The solution is based on three pillars:

Hardware: getting information from vehicle sensors, cameras, other vehicles and road infrastructure;
Android device: interacts with the driver, display video stream, navigation, warnings, etc.;
Cloud platform: gathers data from a vehicles, provides driver with navigation information, road conditions, etc.
Responsibilities:
Take ownership of the hardware components, and needed software;
Prepare documentation and architecture diagrams based on specifications provided by hardware vendor;
Provide consultancy, help client to make right decisions;
Proactivity and fluent collaboration with other teams and internal experts to accomplish features (engineers who work on device part);
Understand business needs and build application accordingly.
Requirements:
Upper-intermediate English;
3+ years of experience C/C++;
Experience in embedded software development and networking;
Ability to explore possibilities of a new sensors and suggest solutions for the product development.
Nice to have:
Experience in C++ 17;
Experience with in V2X, video processing.

