Responsibilities:
- develop and maintain Ruby on Rails web applications using best practices and clean code principles;
- collaborate with the front-end development team to integrate React components into Rails applications;
- design, build and optimize databases using MySQL or MongoDB for efficient data storage and retrieval;
- write and maintain efficient, reusable, and reliable Ruby and JavaScript code;
- ensure the responsiveness and performance of applications by conducting regular testing and debugging;
- deploy and manage applications on AWS;
- stay up-to-date with industry trends and emerging technologies, and propose new ideas for improving development processes.

Requirements:
- proficiency in Ruby on Rails development, with a strong understanding of its conventions and best practices;
- experience in front-end development using React/Angular, JavaScript, HTML and CSS;
- solid understanding of relational databases, particularly PostgreSQL;
- strong problem-solving skills and the ability to work independently or as part of a team;
- excellent communication and collaboration abilities.

Will be a plus:
- knowledge of AWS services and the ability to deploy and manage applications on the AWS platform.

We can offer you:
- outstanding promotion opportunities;
- supportive and comfortable working environment;
- free grammar and vocabulary English on-site courses;
- variety of training and self-development opportunities;
- fancy team-building events and corporate parties;
