Team size: in Ukraine we are creating and looking for 2 Developers at client side they have 2 developers too.
Interviewing:
• 1-st stage: interview with the recruiter (around 30 minutes);
• 2-nd stage: technical interview with a client (around 1 hour);

They are growing and looking for several Ruby on Rails developers to help move their platform for professional on demand e-learning forward. Their products include the verticals ADVOkurser.dk and REVIkurser.dk along with partner sites powered by one monolithic Rails app. 
The hierarchy is flat, individual responsibility is high and micromanagement is non-existent. Joining to their team you will have the possibility to leave your mark on both the code and process.

Skills required:
• At least 2 years of professional experience with Ruby on Rails;
• Experience with APIs and integration of 3rd party services;
• RSpec or similar test framework experience;
• Experience with code reviews, GitHub;
• Client also using rubocop and Code Climate;
• Good written and spoken communications in English.

As a plus:
• Experience with Heroku;

Responsibilities include:
• Collaboratively define and prioritize projects and tasks.
• Develop features for the application.
• Establish stability, safety and productivity in our software environment. (TDD)
• Participate in code reviews and provide thoughtful, constructive feedback for your team.
• Triage, reproduce and debug technical support requests / bugs.

We offer:
• Only interesting and challenging project;
• Clients who are ready and willing to listen to YOUR ideas;
• Work with the skilled team;
• Open management and friendly dynamic team;
• Competitive salary;
• English classes;
• Health and life insurance;
• Practical location and productive environment;
• Make it win-win for you and the company.

Working with us you can expect for:
• Direct communication with a client.
• Work-life balance. No overtimes.
• Beer brewing.
• An opportunity to gain knowledge and add value to ambitious foreign client projects.
• To grow, learn, make a difference — and to have fun!
• To work in a friendly, democratic and transparent company.
• We place high value on building trust, respect and long relationship with our colleagues.

